 Plan: Built-in RateLimiter Dependency
  
 Context

 FastAPI has no built-in rate limiting primitive. Users currently reach for third-party packages
 (slowapi, fastapi-limiter) or write ad-hoc middleware. This plan adds a first-class
 RateLimiter dependency class to the framework itself — composable at route, router, or app
 level, with zero extra dependencies.

 The design exploits two FastAPI internals confirmed by deepsearch + source reading:
 1. Dependency injection — any callable annotated with request: Request has the full
 Starlette request object injected automatically by solve_dependencies() at request time
 (fastapi/dependencies/utils.py:715-716).
 2. Event-loop safety — solve_dependencies is async but the check-and-update path in the
 limiter has no await, so the dict/deque operations are atomic from the event loop's
 perspective. No asyncio.Lock needed.

 User choices: in-memory, sliding window, IP + route path key (with optional
 custom key_func for user/API-key scope), HTTP 429 + Retry-After header.

