 ---
 Implementation

 fastapi/rate_limiting.py (new file)

 Sliding-window rate limiter usable as a FastAPI dependency. Per-instance _store dict;
 share one instance across routes for a shared budget. _default_key respects
 X-Forwarded-For for apps behind a reverse proxy and scopes by route path.

 Usage:
     limiter = RateLimiter(limit=10, window=60)
     @app.get("/items", dependencies=[Depends(limiter)])
     async def list_items(): ...

 ---
 Why dependency, not middleware?

 ┌──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────┐
 │                      │               Dependency (RateLimiter)               │  Middleware (BaseHTTPMiddleware)  │
 ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Granularity          │ Per-route, per-router, or global                     │ Global only                       │
 ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Exception handling   │ Uses FastAPI's ExceptionMiddleware → proper JSON 429 │ Must build JSON response manually │
 ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Access to DI context │ Yes (can compose with auth deps)                     │ No                                │
 ├──────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────┤
 │ Composability        │ Depends() at any level                               │ Registered once on app            │
 └──────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────┘

